The larger 11a1 run improves the first-zero error to \(2.13\times10^{-9}\) at \(x=30,N=120\). Also, 389a1 has an odd minimum at \(x=13\), despite root number \(+1\); parity of the minimum is therefore not a root-number detector.

A further consequence of Lemma `key` strengthens the Q1 result: under even-simple, normalized \(\xi_0\) must be strictly positive. An exact central zero cannot occur in that finite construction.
